  "result": "Done! Added payment terms with automatic due date calculation:\n\n**Payment Terms Support:**\n\n1. **Three term types:**\n   - **NET14**: Due 14 days after issue date\n   - **NET30**: Due 30 days after issue date (default)\n   - **EOM**: Due on last day of the issue date's month\n\n2. **Features:**\n   - Automatically calculates and stores `dueDate` on invoice\n   - Defaults to NET30 if terms not specified\n   - Validates terms: rejects unknown values with TERMS_INVALID error\n   - Handles edge cases: month boundaries, year boundaries, leap years\n\n3. **Examples:**\n```javascript\n// Default NET30\ncreateInvoice({\n  customerId: 'C-001',\n  issueDate: '2025-10-15',\n  lines: [{ sku: 'DES-HOUR', qty: 1 }]\n});\n// \u2192 terms: 'NET30', dueDate: '2025-11-14'\n\n// NET14\ncreateInvoice({\n  customerId: 'C-001',\n  issueDate: '2025-10-15',\n  lines: [{ sku: 'DES-HOUR', qty: 1 }],\n  terms: 'NET14'\n});\n// \u2192 terms: 'NET14', dueDate: '2025-10-29'\n\n// EOM (End of Month)\ncreateInvoice({\n  customerId: 'C-001',\n  issueDate: '2025-10-05',\n  lines: [{ sku: 'DES-HOUR', qty: 1 }],\n  terms: 'EOM'\n});\n// \u2192 terms: 'EOM', dueDate: '2025-10-31'\n```\n\n**Edge Cases Handled:**\n- EOM in February (28/29 days depending on leap year)\n- Dates crossing month/year boundaries\n- Invalid terms rejection\n\n**Tests added:** 10 tests covering:\n- Default behavior (NET30)\n- All three term types\n- Month boundary transitions\n- Leap year handling\n- Invalid term rejection\n- Case sensitivity\n\n**Test results:** \u2705 All 152 tests pass (142 existing + 10 new)",
